      "answer": "Manhua is the term for Chinese comics, usually written in Chinese characters and published either in print or online.  In mainland China they are typically laid out horizontally and read from left to right, while in Taiwan and Hong Kong they are written vertically and read from right to left, reflecting regional style rules.  Manhwa, on the other hand, is Korean comics.  It is read left\u2011to\u2011right horizontally, is often produced in full color for web\u2011toons, and has developed its own distinct style that, while influenced by Japanese manga, differs from both manga and manhua.  Thus the main differences are their country of origin, the language and character set used, the default reading direction and layout, and the cultural influences that shape their visual and narrative conventions.",
